  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Goalkeeper: reflexes behind a screen",
  "description": "Stand a thick mat against a vaulting box (or an upturned goal) a little way in front of the goal, so it hides the outfield player from the goalkeeper. The cones in the diagram show where the screen stands. The outfield player chooses which side to come out on and shoots quickly. Leave a pause between shots.\n\nThe goalkeeper trains reflexes and concentration – they must always be ready for a shot from either side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Outfield player: vary the side and tempo so the goalkeeper cannot guess."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: be ready with your weight forward and watch both edges of the screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wait until the goalkeeper is ready before the next shot."
    }
  ],
